{#-
  The ratings widget (SPEC §12, §15.1) and a closed solution card's summary
  line. src/js/rating.js makes them work; the layouts load it only while
  site.features.ratings is exactly true, and render these only then:

    {% from "partials/rating.njk" import rating, ratingStatus %}
    {% if site.features.ratings === true %}{{ rating(video, 'row') }}{% endif %}

  rating(video, variant)  the widget, under a video and before its
                          FormatLinks. variant: 'row' (problem video, Start
                          here bar: the legend beside the stars where there
                          is room) or 'card' (an open solution card: the
                          legend above them)
  ratingStatus(video)     a closed solution card's summary line, in its meta
                          row: "You rated this n of 5." once a rating is
                          accepted (rating.js), else empty and hidden

  Both ship `hidden`: without JavaScript there is nothing to show (a form
  POST can't reach the API, which takes JSON), and rating.js reveals them
  once it is listening. A wrapper that would hold only the widget carries
  `hidden data-rating-reveal`, and rating.js reveals it too.

  The widget: a <fieldset> whose legend is "Was this helpful?" plus the
  video's title for screen readers (a problem page has up to seven), five
  native radios ("1 star" to "5 stars"; arrow keys move between them, and
  autocomplete="off" so a browser doesn't restore an old choice) with each
  <label> a 44x44px star; the status line, empty until there is news
  (decision a2 = B), its height reserved by hidden copies of the longest
  messages so the answer never shifts the page; then the §15.1 notice.
  `data-rating` names the video: pages.json reads it (SPEC §8.3), and
  rating.js sends it. ids are unique per page: the validator allows each
  video once per page.
-#}
{%- from "partials/icons.njk" import icon -%}
{%- macro rating(video, variant='row') -%}
{%- set id = video.video_id -%}
<div class="rating rating--{{ variant }}" data-rating="{{ id }}" hidden>
  <fieldset class="rating__group">
    <legend class="rating__legend">Was this helpful?<span class="visually-hidden"> {{ video.title }}</span></legend>
    <div class="rating__stars">
      {%- for n in range(1, 6) %}
      <input class="rating__input visually-hidden" type="radio" name="rating-{{ id }}" id="rating-{{ id }}-{{ n }}" value="{{ n }}" autocomplete="off">
      <label class="rating__star" for="rating-{{ id }}-{{ n }}">{{ icon('star', 28 if variant == 'card' else 26, 'rating__icon') }}<span class="visually-hidden">{{ n }} star{{ 's' if n > 1 }}</span></label>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </fieldset>
  <div class="rating__status-box">
    <p class="rating__status" id="rating-{{ id }}-status" data-rating-status></p>
    <p class="rating__sizer" aria-hidden="true">Thanks. You rated this 5 of 5.</p>
    <p class="rating__sizer" aria-hidden="true">Couldn't send right now — please try again later</p>
  </div>
  {% include "notices/ratings.njk" -%}
</div>
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro ratingStatus(video) -%}
<p class="solution__rating" data-rating-summary="{{ video.video_id }}" hidden></p>
{%- endmacro -%}
